Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:20:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] IAU 2000B on the linear terms of its arguments, as published
 (UPSTREAM-BUGS 233, G162, G140, G24)

The published IAU 2000B (McCarthy & Luzum 2003; SOFA iauNut00b, NOVAS
iau2000b) takes the Delaunay arguments' linear terms alone; the library's
2000B was its 2000A function with the loop cut short, on the full Simon
et al. polynomials to T^4. Against the published model in mpmath (which
reproduces SOFA's test values to 5e-24 rad), dpsi 5.9e-10 deg off at
2006, 7.4e-9 at 2023, 2.9e-8 at 1900, 1.6e-7 at 2100, 1.4e-5 at AD 1000,
1.5e-4 at -1000; SOFA's test value at TT 2006 Jan 1 1.02e-11 rad. Both
builds.

The trade-off, against the library's IAU 2000A over -3000..3000 (dpsi
worst, mas): the polynomials 3.7, 3.6, 2.0, 2.7, 2.0, 2.1, 2.3 over
-3000..-1000, ..1000, ..1800, ..1995, ..2050, ..2200, ..3000; the
published linear terms 1440, 537, 62.3, 3.4, 2.1, 3.5, 65.1. Equal over
1995-2050, where the model claims its milliarcsecond; far from 2000 the
published model is its own approximation, up to 1.44" off 2000A at
-3000. No Swiss Ephemeris document gives a reason for the polynomials
(swisseph.doc 3, swephprg's 1.70 changes, swephexp.h's "fast, but
precision of milli-arcsec"), and the fork's default is 2000A, so 2000B is
the published model now, as entry 220 made its offsets.

calc_nutation_iau2000ab() takes the linear terms under
SEMOD_NUT_IAU_2000B, past 4e8 days in double-double
(nut_ls_args_linear_exact(), entry 188's table to its T term), and
calc_nutation_2000b_rate() the same arguments with their constant rates.
2000A and the default unchanged bit for bit. Behind #ifndef
SWE_UPSTREAM_COMPAT: the compat build's default keeps upstream's values.

After: within 2.5e-15 deg of the published model at -1000..3500; SOFA's
test values to 1.1e-19 rad.

G162 tests/nutseries.c check (c) against the published model (table
regenerated) within 1e-13 deg, 2.5e-15, and SOFA's test values within
1e-17 rad (was 3e-11), 1.07e-19; check (f) adds 2000B's rate past 4e8
(1.6e-14, 3.1e-14 deg/day): 89 pass; before 232 and 233, 10 fail; the
upstream build 81 of its 81. G140 tests/nutderiv.c's long double 2000B
reference on the linear arguments (1.58e-13 deg). G24 nut00b_linear_off:
2000B at AD 1000 and -1000 against the published model, 2.5e-15 deg
shipped (1.51e-4 before), 1.51e-4 compat; nut00b_sofa_off now within
1e-17 rad shipped (1.07e-19), 1.88e-9 compat. G1's cov:nutmodel[4]
(J2000) does not move; G139's 0,8,8,4 rows move within their limits.
G122, G139 and check-compat pass.

Files: swephlib.c, sweph.h, tests/nutseries.c, tests/nutderiv.c,
tests/compat.c, notes/UPSTREAM-BUGS.md, notes/REVIEW.md.
